From: natemu <natemu@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] FEXCore: slice1 no stop check at block entry

Under fexc_slice1 only: EmitSuspendInterruptCheck emits nothing (patch 0011
emitted the placeholder `bl .` the resident relocated to its stop pad). The
resident now stops a running vCPU by IRQ-triggered unlinking: its interrupt
handler patches every exit of the block it interrupted, so nothing is left
on the hot path. The default profile is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp
@@ -803,10 +803,8 @@ void Arm64JITCore::EmitTFCheck() {
 
 void Arm64JITCore::EmitSuspendInterruptCheck() {
   if (fexc_slice1) {
-    // natemu slice1: `bl` to the vCPU's stop pad (a `ret` alone in its stage-2 granule), relocated by the resident when it
-    // places the block. A kick removes execute permission from the pad, so the next block entry stops precisely there.
-    // x30 is an RA temporary, dead at a block entry.
-    dc32(0x94000000);
+    // natemu slice1: no stop check. The resident stops a running vCPU by unlinking: its interrupt handler patches the
+    // exits of the block it interrupted (nothing on the hot path).
     return;
   }
   if (CTX->Config.NeedsPendingInterruptFaultCheck) {
